From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of join_order_operator.cpp as used

join_order_operator.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (rule),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/join_order/join_order_operator.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/join_order/join_order_operator.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/join_order/join_order_operator.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/join_order/join_order_operator.cpp
@@ -269,6 +269,7 @@ void JoinOrderConflictDetector::Build(vector<unique_ptr<JoinOrderOperator>> &ope
 		SimplifyConflictRules(*op, set_manager);
 		D_ASSERT(ContainedInUnion(op->total_set, op->left_relations, op->right_relations));
 		for (auto &rule : op->conflict_rules) {
+			(void)rule;
 			D_ASSERT(ContainedInUnion(rule.trigger, op->left_relations, op->right_relations));
 			D_ASSERT(ContainedInUnion(rule.requirement, op->left_relations, op->right_relations));
 		}
